# Legacy CMS URL repair. These sites are static exports of the old Omeka
# installs, and the export appended .html to every page: /items/show/60 became
# /items/show/60.html. Everything indexed or cited before the migration points
# at the extensionless form. Proven on occupyarchive.org: 272 redirects, 190
# hits.
#
# Ordering matters — Caddy runs `redir` before `handle`, so this fires ahead of
# the object-storage matcher. Never put /files/... in this map; those are served
# live from Garage and a redirect would shadow them.
@needs_html {
    not path *.*   # already has an extension: .html (no loop), assets, Garage /files/*
    not path */    # directories already resolve to index.html
}

# {path} drops the query, so every /items/browse?advanced[0][…] facet collapses
# to /items/browse.html. Right call, but add an explicit entry if the export
# never captured that page.
#
# NOT for Hugo sites — those need /foo/, not /foo.html, and this would 301 them
# into a 404.
redir @needs_html {path}.html 301
